<title>ISRAEL: Israel M1 money supply up 0.1 pct in August.</title>
<headline>Israel M1 money supply up 0.1 pct in August.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's M1 money supply rose 0.1 percent in August to 16.64 billion shekels, the Bank of Israel said.</p>
<p>		    August 96	July 96     August 95</p>
<p>M1		  +0.1 pct	 +4.1 pct    +3.0 pct</p>
<p>Total credit    +0.3 pct	 +1.8 pct    +1.4 pct</p>
<p>Credit to the public totalled 237.2 billion shekels in August 1996.</p>
<p>In the first eight months of 1996 M1 rose 9.6 percent.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.17 shekels)</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
